        "id": "MON-01",
        "severity": "high",
        "state": "active intermittent",
        "title": "GPU exporter repeatedly fails liveness and its pod memory cap causes severe historical page-cache thrashing",
        "evidence": "482 restarts at initial snapshot; approximately 158 per 24 hours and 7 per hour. Readiness /health timeouts 4,409 and liveness restart events 418; scrape success 68.7% of samples over 24 hours. DCGM pod cgroup has a 512 MiB cap, 161,240,668 memory.max boundary events, 9.62 billion file refaults, 7,916,628 major faults, and 39.48 TB read from node device 8:0 since pod creation September 3 05:47Z. Total full memory stall time is 6,277 seconds. OOM kills are zero; liveness kills explain exit 137. A freshly restarted container looked quiet because the restrictive pod parent retains the history and generates the limit events.",
        "recommendation": "Treat DCGM as a second confirmed historical read-thrashing source alongside recovery-server. Repair memory sizing at both pod and container levels through GitOps and verify reduced refault/read/stall rates plus sustained exporter health. Current restarted child had low I/O and zero PSI, so the lifetime total is not the current rate. Preserve NVIDIA hardware health conclusions separately; exporter failure alone does not mean GPU failure.",
